{"id": "recology-payments-for-rates", "title": "Recology admitted bribing its regulator and refunded $94.5M in disputed rates", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.179, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "b2dab4292af45ab2", "words": 386, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Recology collects San Francisco’s garbage. The City sets what it can charge every household.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.54, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Recology", "sub": "San Francisco’s garbage collector"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.51, 0.78, 0.93, 1.48, 2.15, 2.55, 2.77, 3.0, 3.1, 3.22, 3.35, 3.56, 3.79]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[5]"], "text": "The man over those rates was Public Works director Mohammed Nuru.", "t0": 4.66, "t1": 8.01, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "keeping him happy is important"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.35, 0.6, 0.83, 1.16, 1.36, 1.7, 1.97, 2.38, 2.84]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[5]"], "text": "In 2015, a Recology manager wrote: keeping him happy is important.", "t0": 8.13, "t1": 12.52, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "keeping him happy is important"}, "emph": ["keeping him happy"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.3, 0.83, 0.92, 1.38, 1.74, 2.31, 2.95, 3.15, 3.4, 3.49]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount", "established[2]"], "text": "So how much did Recology spend on him, in hidden gifts?", "t0": 12.64, "t1": 15.47, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Disguised benefits", "sub": "2014 to January 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.23, 0.43, 0.58, 1.11, 1.35, 1.52, 1.87, 2.01, 2.35]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[2]"], "text": "More than 900,000 dollars.", "t0": 15.47, "t1": 17.6, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$900,000", "label": "more than, per the U.S. Attorney"}, "emph": ["More"], "wt": [0.04, 0.45, 0.61, 0.86, 1.14, 1.51]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "That’s proven. Three Recology companies admitted the bribery scheme.", "t0": 18.12, "t1": 21.79, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Admitted", "sub": "a deferred prosecution agreement, 2021"}, "emph": ["admitted"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.72, 1.34, 1.81, 2.22, 2.6, 2.7, 3.1]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "First, the biggest piece.", "t0": 22.01, "t1": 23.4, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "$150,000 a year"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "SF Clean City Coalition", "sub": "kept about 5 percent"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "at the Parks Alliance, Nuru could spend"}], "kicker": "How the money moved"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.53, 0.84]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "Recology gave a nonprofit 150,000 dollars a year, in 30,000-dollar payments.", "t0": 23.52, "t1": 28.34, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "$150,000 a year"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "SF Clean City Coalition", "sub": "kept about 5 percent"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "at the Parks Alliance, Nuru could spend"}], "kicker": "How the money moved"}, "emph": ["150,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.59, 0.68, 1.2, 1.34, 1.62, 1.88, 2.23, 2.56, 2.65, 3.18, 3.31, 3.57, 4.14]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[4]"], "text": "Why route it through charities? So nothing showed on City books.", "t0": 28.46, "t1": 32.26, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "$150,000 a year"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "SF Clean City Coalition", "sub": "kept about 5 percent"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "at the Parks Alliance, Nuru could spend"}], "kicker": "How the money moved"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.43, 0.5, 0.74, 1.67, 2.34, 2.62, 2.87, 2.97, 3.26]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[4]"], "text": "The money passed on to accounts Nuru could spend.", "t0": 32.38, "t1": 34.53, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "$150,000 a year"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "SF Clean City Coalition", "sub": "kept about 5 percent"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works accounts", "sub": "at the Parks Alliance, Nuru could spend"}], "kicker": "How the money moved"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.34, 0.61, 0.73, 0.82, 1.21, 1.47, 1.66]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Next: 60,000 dollars of holiday donations to a kids’ charity.", "t0": 34.65, "t1": 38.08, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Holiday donations", "sub": "Lefty O’Doul’s Foundation for Kids, 2016 to 2019", "chip": "$60,000"}, "emph": ["60,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.8, 1.08, 1.4, 1.49, 1.84, 2.38, 2.5, 2.6, 3.1]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "It paid for Nuru’s staff holiday parties.", "t0": 38.2, "t1": 40.16, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Holiday donations", "sub": "Lefty O’Doul’s Foundation for Kids, 2016 to 2019", "chip": "$60,000"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.24, 0.37, 0.79, 1.06, 1.42]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]", "established[12]"], "text": "And his son got a job, about 19,565 dollars.", "t0": 40.28, "t1": 43.96, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["his son’s job, 2015–2017", "about $19,565"], "b": ["paid internship, 2017–2018", "about $23,600"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.44, 0.58, 0.69, 1.05, 1.26, 1.6, 2.02, 2.27, 2.58, 3.11]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]", "established[12]"], "text": "Then a paid internship, about 23,600.", "t0": 44.08, "t1": 46.81, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["his son’s job, 2015–2017", "about $19,565"], "b": ["paid internship, 2017–2018", "about $23,600"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.13, 0.4, 1.08, 1.33, 1.68, 2.05, 2.29]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[13]"], "text": "Court papers add more: 3,500 dollars for a staff funeral, and New York hotel rooms.", "t0": 46.93, "t1": 52.53, "shot": "b10a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Not in the releases", "kicker": "The court papers", "sub": "$3,500 for a funeral, June 2016; hotel rooms at $865.34 each, December 2017"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.54, 0.75, 1.16, 1.83, 2.26, 2.55, 2.78, 3.11, 3.28, 3.39, 3.67, 4.38, 4.46, 4.61, 4.81, 5.12]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]", "established[5]"], "text": "Now the rates.", "t0": 52.75, "t1": 53.58, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The 2017 rate increase", "kicker": "The rates"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]", "established[5]"], "text": "Recology’s 2017 request to raise household rates was approved, while the payments flowed.", "t0": 53.7, "t1": 58.36, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The 2017 rate increase", "kicker": "The rates"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 0.68, 1.15, 1.49, 1.62, 1.83, 2.24, 2.5, 2.66, 3.44, 3.59, 3.73, 4.1]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]", "established[5]"], "text": "The City later said it had an error. How much does the City call overcharges?", "t0": 58.48, "t1": 62.82, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The 2017 rate increase", "kicker": "The rates"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.37, 0.58, 0.77, 0.85, 1.0, 1.14, 1.75, 2.55, 2.76, 2.94, 3.03, 3.24, 3.52]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]"], "text": "86.6 million dollars.", "t0": 62.82, "t1": 65.48, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$86.6 million", "label": "repaid to ratepayers, plus $7.9 million interest"}, "emph": ["86.6"], "wt": [0.04, 1.02, 1.41, 1.61, 2.04]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[7]", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "Recology paid it back, plus interest and 7 million to the City.", "t0": 66.0, "t1": 69.87, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no admission that the companies overcharged"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.7, 0.8, 1.21, 1.48, 2.0, 2.35, 2.63, 3.03, 3.14, 3.26]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[7]", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "But in a civil settlement, it denied overcharging. No court has found it did.", "t0": 69.99, "t1": 74.34, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no admission that the companies overcharged"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.27, 0.37, 0.59, 1.27, 1.41, 1.76, 2.96, 3.11, 3.43, 3.57, 3.82, 3.97]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "Recology set aside 25 million more for ratepayers.", "t0": 74.46, "t1": 77.52, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$23.4 million", "label": "more profit above the 9 percent margin"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.51, 0.66, 0.92, 1.4, 1.75, 2.02, 2.23]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Was the error caused by the bribes? No finding says so. The City’s own reviewers missed it.", "t0": 77.64, "t1": 83.04, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the City’s own reviewers missed it"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.2, 0.42, 0.73, 0.79, 0.92, 1.75, 1.97, 2.32, 2.61, 2.98, 3.33, 3.61, 3.82, 4.34, 4.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[18]"], "text": "A 2021 criminal complaint says Nuru approved Recology drawing over 10 million dollars of rate money.", "t0": 83.16, "t1": 88.69, "shot": "b15a", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Nuru approved Recology’s requests for more than $10 million of the Zero Waste Incentive Funds", "kicker": "The complaint against Porter, 13 April 2021 · not part of a plea"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.28, 0.81, 1.1, 1.57, 1.8, 2.13, 2.6, 3.14, 3.55, 3.82, 4.03, 4.5, 4.88, 4.98, 5.24]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[3]"], "text": "The companies’ criminal penalty: 36 million dollars.", "t0": 88.91, "t1": 91.9, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$36 million", "label": "criminal penalty, including the $7 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.45, 0.75, 1.51, 2.08, 2.39]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]", "story[4]"], "text": "Two managers, Paul Giusti and John Porter, pleaded guilty.", "t0": 92.02, "t1": 95.08, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Paul Giusti and John Porter", "sub": "pleaded guilty"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.72, 0.93, 1.3, 1.41, 1.68, 2.14, 2.44]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]", "story[4]", "established[14]"], "text": "Each got three years of probation and a 30,000-dollar fine.", "t0": 95.2, "t1": 98.27, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Paul Giusti and John Porter", "sub": "pleaded guilty"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.44, 0.66, 0.91, 1.0, 1.54, 1.73, 1.79, 2.01, 2.66]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[10]"], "text": "One more. The Environment Department’s head also asked Recology for money.", "t0": 98.49, "t1": 102.22, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Department of the Environment", "kicker": "One more", "sub": "2015 and 2019 contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.7, 0.91, 1.26, 1.76, 2.09, 2.35, 2.63, 3.09, 3.23]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[10]"], "text": "Both times, just before signing its contracts, in 2015 and 2019.", "t0": 102.34, "t1": 106.64, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Department of the Environment", "kicker": "One more", "sub": "2015 and 2019 contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.67, 0.86, 1.08, 1.41, 1.57, 2.3, 2.42, 2.67, 3.28, 3.51, 3.74]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "established[11]"], "text": "The company deal wasn’t a conviction.", "t0": 106.86, "t1": 108.83, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["A conviction of the companies"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.47, 0.84, 1.32, 1.4]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "established[11]", "established[15]"], "text": "The federal charge was dropped in October 2024 once its terms were met.", "t0": 108.95, "t1": 112.99, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["A conviction of the companies"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.02, 0.36, 0.69, 0.83, 1.17, 1.31, 1.64, 1.91, 2.59, 3.08, 3.29, 3.6, 3.78]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["established[9]", "next[0]"], "text": "Recology is now barred from gifts to City staff.", "t0": 113.11, "t1": 115.67, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "A year-by-year Giant Sweep breakdown"}, {"who": "", "what": "The Clean City Coalition’s ledger"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.55, 0.71, 1.08, 1.25, 1.58, 1.72, 2.02]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["established[2]", "next[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Their statement of facts puts Giant Sweep alone at about 900,000 dollars, but not year by year.", "t0": 115.79, "t1": 121.53, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "A year-by-year Giant Sweep breakdown"}, {"who": "", "what": "The Clean City Coalition’s ledger"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.4, 0.51, 0.9, 1.18, 1.5, 1.8, 2.21, 2.39, 2.68, 2.99, 3.27, 3.69, 4.6, 4.72, 4.96, 5.17, 5.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Resolved: bribery admitted, a 36 million penalty, and 25 million more set aside.", "t0": 121.65, "t1": 127.14, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.84, 1.19, 2.08, 2.19, 2.6, 2.96, 3.53, 3.62, 4.09, 4.45, 4.71, 4.94]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.26, "t1": 129.43, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.6, 0.78, 1.06, 1.16, 1.27, 1.54, 1.82]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "Proven · the payments", "lead1": "The rates · $86.6 million", "lead2": "The penalties", "lead3": "Another department", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "contrast"}